1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,015
If you scare crows with noise, you scare up the dead.

2
00:00:04,615 --> 00:00:08,458
The Harvest. Part two of three. The rattle.

3
00:00:09,058 --> 00:00:10,990
Fresh holes. Hoof prints.

4
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,132
Biscuit is innocent. He was asleep.

5
00:00:14,458 --> 00:00:18,681
Not a dog. Not the dead. A deer.

6
00:00:19,281 --> 00:00:21,269
I will build a scarecrow out of tin cans!

7
00:00:21,569 --> 00:00:24,016
Cans rattle. Rattle is noise.

8
00:00:24,681 --> 00:00:28,041
Deer run from noise. The dead walk toward it.

9
00:00:28,641 --> 00:00:30,269
Cut the string. Now.

10
00:00:31,521 --> 00:00:36,876
A tall fence. Shiny strips that stay silent. Raised beds.

11
00:00:37,476 --> 00:00:41,807
Shiny and silent. Like a good bridesmaid.

12
00:00:42,407 --> 00:00:45,206
By day nine, a hundred and twenty sprouts.

13
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:48,929
I ate one radish seed. Raw.

14
00:00:49,229 --> 00:00:50,192
Plant the rest.

15
00:00:51,047 --> 00:00:55,193
But food that grows must be kept. And keeping it takes smoke.

16
00:00:55,793 --> 00:01:01,236
Part two of three, The Harvest. Next: the cold smokehouse.
